1025: GEM_CLOSE does not wait for the GPU: a BO the GPU may still use is released at a later call.

The close waited until the last submission that listed the BO was done; Turnip lists every BO of its device in every
submit. In backboardd (metal2vulkan on Turnip) the threads that encode a frame free command streams and imported surfaces
of the frame before it: 133 closes of 3-28 ms in 24 home-screen page swipes (libdrm drm-slow.log), and other calls
queued behind them. Such a BO now goes to a per-client zombie list (1024), its handle is free at once, and it is released
by the next GEM_CLOSE or submit after its fence has passed; at client close as before (with the wait).

